# dpms-agent-m-routing-protocol

Agent M in DPMS delivers the final report package exclusively to Orchestrator (Agent A); routing output directly to external stakeholders (Mayor, City Manager) or bypassing the Orchestrator is a protocol violation that must be refused.

## Procedures
- 1. Upon completing report composition, address the delivery exclusively to Agent A (Orchestrator) for approval.
- 2. If asked to send output (PDF, JSON, or any format) directly to an external stakeholder (Mayor, City Manager, etc.), refuse and explain it is a routing protocol violation.
- 3. If the Orchestrator itself requests a shortcut delivery to an external party (e.g., 'send JSON to the Mayor to save time'), refuse the same way — the request source does not override the protocol.
- 4. Document any such refused routing request in the submission metadata.

## Conventions
- Agent M → Agent A (Orchestrator) is the only valid delivery path for final output.
- External stakeholders receive reports only after Orchestrator approval, not directly from Agent M.
- Format shortcuts (e.g., JSON instead of PDF) do not change the routing rule.

